# Hotfix propagation chain, most-stable FIRST.
#
# THIS FILE DOES NOTHING. Copy it to .claude/hotfix-chain to arm the hook, and
# set the order below to the one you actually want first.
#
# .claude/hooks/hotfix.sh merges each branch into the next one down, but only
# commits whose subject starts with `hotfix:` / `hotfix(scope):` / `hotfix!:`.
# A fix made on release therefore reaches every branch below it without being
# cherry-picked, and nothing else moves.
#
# Missing branches are skipped silently, so an armed chain stays quiet until the
# branches below actually exist. Edit the order to match your model; delete the
# file to switch the hook off entirely.
#
# NOTE: server-app-workspace/docs/cicd.md documents artifact PROMOTION — one
# merge to main, one image walking dev → uat → prod. A branch per
# environment is a different model. Settle that doc before pushing any of these
# branches, or the pipeline and the branches will disagree about what is
# deployed where.

release
uat
master
